{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"Boxed-warning text present, but current source metadata cites FDA/DailyMed SPL and a DailyMed URL.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2026/018723Orig1s073%3B%20019680Orig1s060%3B%20021168Orig1s052ltr.pdf"],"proposed_value":"Keep boxed-warning text; replace source metadata with FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; effective_time=20260331; title=DEPAKOTE ER / DIVALPROEX SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","rationale":"The boxed warning content is concordant with FDA labeling/openFDA, but DailyMed is not permissible for the black-box source field under the audit policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"GI: nausea 48%, CNS: somnolence 27%, neurologic: tremor 25%, CNS: dizziness 25%, GI: vomiting 23%, dermatologic: alopecia 6%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"GI: nausea 48%, CNS: somnolence 27%, neurologic: tremor 25%, CNS: dizziness 25%, GI: vomiting 27%, dermatologic: alopecia 6%","rationale":"The FDA Depakote ER label adverse-reaction table supporting the other listed percentages reports vomiting at 27%, not 23%.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium","rationale":"These are valproate active-moiety names/salts or related non-US naming variants. Consolidating them under the valproic-acid active-moiety row is appropriate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/referrals/valproate-related-substances","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/6102/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA lists valproate products approved in the US, including Depakene, Depakote, Depakote ER, Depakote CP, and Depacon.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information"]},{"current_value":"Enzyme inhibitor: inhibits UGT, epoxide hydrolase, and some CYP pathways; not an inducer","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Enzyme inhibitor: inhibits UGT, epoxide hydrolase, and some CYP pathways; not an inducer","rationale":"FDA labeling supports clinically relevant inhibition of metabolism/protein binding interactions, and NCBI/PubMed literature supports UGT, epoxide hydrolase, and CYP inhibition. The row's inhibitor classification is supported.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15492760/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"Focal; Generalized; Absence; Myoclonic; Generalized tonic-clonic; Mixed seizure types","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal; Generalized; Absence; Myoclonic; Generalized tonic-clonic; Mixed seizure types","rationale":"FDA labeling supports complex partial/focal seizures, simple and complex absence seizures, and multiple seizure types that include absence. NCBI/Epilepsy Foundation sources support broader generalized seizure types including myoclonic and tonic-clonic use.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/","https://www.epilepsy.com/tools-resources/seizure-medication-list/valproic-acid"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Valproate Information page; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed/PMC RCT reports; ClinicalTrials.gov","rationale":"DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification and Epilepsy Society is outside the allowed trusted-source domain list. Replace with trusted FDA, NCBI/PubMed/PMC, and ClinicalTrials.gov sources that support the row facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; published=Apr 13, 2026; title=DEPAKOTE ER (DIVALPROEX SODIUM) TABLET, EXTENDED RELEASE [ABBVIE INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; effective_time=20260331; title=DEPAKOTE ER / DIVALPROEX SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","rationale":"The current source uses DailyMed, which is explicitly not permitted for black-box-warning verification. FDA/openFDA is permitted.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; oral solution/syrup; delayed-release tablet; extended-release tablet; sprinkle capsule; IV injection","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Capsule; oral solution/syrup; delayed-release tablet; extended-release tablet; sprinkle capsule; IV injection","rationale":"FDA sources list oral capsules/solution, delayed-release tablets, extended-release tablets, sprinkle capsules, and IV valproate sodium injection products.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"9-16 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"9-16 h","rationale":"FDA labeling reports mean terminal half-life for valproate monotherapy ranging from 9 to 16 hours after oral dosing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"FDA labeling describes valproate as metabolized almost entirely by the liver.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"60 mg/kg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"60 mg/kg/day","rationale":"FDA seizure dosing specifies increases up to a maximum recommended dosage of 60 mg/kg/day.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"FDA labeling states the mechanisms are not established but suggests increased brain GABA concentrations; literature describes additional proposed mechanisms. Moderate confidence is reasonable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"Dissociates to valproate; mechanisms are not established, but FDA labeling suggests antiseizure activity may relate to increased brain GABA concentrations. Additional ion-channel effects are proposed but not definitive.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Dissociates to valproate; mechanisms are not established, but FDA labeling suggests antiseizure activity may relate to increased brain GABA concentrations. Additional ion-channel effects are proposed but not definitive.","rationale":"This accurately reflects FDA labeling and review-level mechanism descriptions.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls mechanism review","rationale":"The mechanism fact can be supported without DailyMed by FDA/accessdata labeling and NCBI Bookshelf. This also aligns with the trusted-source-domain policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label","rationale":"The core mechanism statement is explicitly anchored in FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"10-15 mg/kg/day initial; titrate to clinical response","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"10-15 mg/kg/day initial; titrate to clinical response","rationale":"FDA seizure dosing supports starting at 10 to 15 mg/kg/day for complex partial seizures and 15 mg/kg/day for absence seizures, with titration by response.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium; Depacon; Depakote; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakene; Depakine; Epilim; Epival","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"valproate; divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium; Depacon; Depakote; Depakote CP; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkle Capsules; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakene; Depakine; Epilim; Epival","rationale":"Add standalone valproate and FDA-listed Depakote CP/Depakote Sprinkle Capsules variants to improve alias coverage. Existing aliases are appropriate for the consolidated active-moiety row.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/referrals/valproate-related-substances"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","rationale":"No trusted row source specifically supports a QT-effect conclusion. The statement is plausible as an absence-of-established-effect claim, but it should not be treated as source-verified from the current evidence_sources.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":[]},{"current_value":"Convulex; Depacon; Depakene; Depakine; Depakote; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakyn; Dyzantil; Epilim Chrono; Epilim Chronosphere; Epival; Stavzor; Valproate Sodium","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Convulex; Depacon; Depakene; Depakine; Depakote; Depakote CP; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkle Capsules; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakyn; Dyzantil; Epilim Chrono; Epilim Chronosphere; Epival; Stavzor; Valproate Sodium","rationale":"FDA sources support Depacon, Depakene, Depakote, Depakote ER, Depakote CP, and valproate sodium products; EMA/eMC sources support non-US brands such as Convulex, Depakine, Dyzantil, and Epilim variants. Depakyn and Epival were not independently verified from the allowed source set in this pass, but no direct contradiction was found, so they are retained.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/referrals/valproate-related-substances","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/6102/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy: 10-60 mg/kg/day depending on valproate formulation; IV valproate sodium may substitute for oral valproate when oral therapy is temporarily not feasible.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Epilepsy: 10-60 mg/kg/day depending on valproate formulation; IV valproate sodium may substitute for oral valproate when oral therapy is temporarily not feasible.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports seizure dosing from 10-15 mg/kg/day initial titration up to 60 mg/kg/day and IV valproate sodium as an alternative when oral therapy is temporarily not feasible.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"1978 valproic acid; 1983 divalproex sodium; Dec 30, 1996 valproate sodium injection","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1978 valproic acid; 1983 divalproex sodium; Dec 30, 1996 valproate sodium injection","rationale":"FDA/NCBI sources support initial approval years for valproic acid, divalproex sodium, and valproate sodium injection. The exact Dec 30, 1996 date should be tied to Drugs@FDA/openFDA application metadata rather than the Depakote ER label alone.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/","https://api.fda.gov/drug/drugsfda.json?search=application_number:%22NDA020593%22"]}],"generic_name":"valproic acid","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"19 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Willmore1996 add-on divalproex sodium/valproate 19%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Willmore1996 add-on divalproex sodium 19%)","rationale":"Willmore1996 reports RR50 of 38% for divalproex sodium versus 19% for placebo, giving a 19 percentage-point differential. The current value is numerically correct; the proposed wording uses the trial drug name exactly.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"]},{"current_value":"Willmore1996|19|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/|137","field":"plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Willmore1996|19|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/|137","rationale":"The plotted effect size and intent-to-treat n=137 match the PubMed abstract and local outcome audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"Willmore1996 reports median absolute seizure-count reduction, not median percent change. Richens1975 and Sharshar2023 do not provide extractable active/placebo MPC percentages in the cited records.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1104059/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36624526/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"Willmore1996 reports seizure-free counts for complex partial seizures, but not a directly extractable patient-rate differential in the cited abstract. Richens1975 and Sharshar2023 do not provide extractable seizure-freedom percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1104059/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36624526/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"GI: nausea 48%, CNS: somnolence 27%, neurologic: tremor 25%, CNS: dizziness 25%, GI: vomiting 23%, dermatologic: alopecia 6%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"GI: nausea 48%, CNS: somnolence 27%, neurologic: tremor 25%, CNS: dizziness 25%, GI: vomiting 27%, dermatologic: alopecia 6%","reason":"FDA label table supporting the listed adverse-event percentages reports vomiting 27%.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; published=Apr 13, 2026; title=DEPAKOTE ER (DIVALPROEX SODIUM) TABLET, EXTENDED RELEASE [ABBVIE INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; effective_time=20260331; title=DEPAKOTE ER / DIVALPROEX SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","reason":"Black-box source must be FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA only; DailyMed is not permissible.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Valproate Information page; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed/PMC RCT reports; ClinicalTrials.gov","reason":"Use only trusted-source domains and remove DailyMed/Epilepsy Society as row support sources for this audit context.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls mechanism review","reason":"The mechanism statement is supported by trusted FDA and NCBI sources without using DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]},{"current_value":"19 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Willmore1996 add-on divalproex sodium/valproate 19%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Willmore1996 add-on divalproex sodium 19%)","reason":"Numerically correct, but the RCT intervention was divalproex sodium; this wording is more exact.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"]},{"current_value":"divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium; Depacon; Depakote; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakene; Depakine; Epilim; Epival","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"valproate; divalproex sodium; sodium valproate; valproate semisodium; valproate sodium; Depacon; Depakote; Depakote CP; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkle Capsules; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakene; Depakine; Epilim; Epival","reason":"Add standalone valproate and FDA-listed Depakote CP/Depakote Sprinkle Capsules variants.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information"]},{"current_value":"Convulex; Depacon; Depakene; Depakine; Depakote; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakyn; Dyzantil; Epilim Chrono; Epilim Chronosphere; Epival; Stavzor; Valproate Sodium","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Convulex; Depacon; Depakene; Depakine; Depakote; Depakote CP; Depakote ER; Depakote Sprinkle Capsules; Depakote Sprinkles; Depakyn; Dyzantil; Epilim Chrono; Epilim Chronosphere; Epival; Stavzor; Valproate Sodium","reason":"Add FDA-listed Depakote CP and formal Depakote Sprinkle Capsules alias; retain uncontradicted existing names.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/referrals/valproate-related-substances","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/6102/smpc"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Willmore1996","pmid":"8559420","proposed_action":"Keep as qualifying RCT link.","rationale":"PubMed verifies the PMID/title. The abstract reports add-on divalproex sodium, a placebo group, randomized controlled trial publication type, and extractable RR50 values of 38% active versus 19% placebo.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"},{"label":"Richens1975","pmid":"1104059","proposed_action":"Keep as qualifying RCT link.","rationale":"PubMed/PMC verify sodium valproate in severe epilepsy, randomized/double-blind crossover design, and placebo control. No RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom percentages are extractable from the cited abstract.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1104059/"},{"label":"Sharshar2023","pmid":"36624526","proposed_action":"Keep as qualifying RCT link, but do not use for RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom summary values.","rationale":"PubMed/PMC and ClinicalTrials.gov verify valproic acid as adjuvant treatment for convulsive status epilepticus in a randomized placebo-controlled clinical trial. The cited record does not supply extractable RR50, MPC, or seizure-freedom patient-rate differentials.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36624526/"},{"label":"McGuire1988 candidate","pmid":"3130256","proposed_action":"Do not add to pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links.","rationale":"Although the record is randomized/placebo-controlled, it is a haem-biosynthesis/porphyria safety/pharmacology study in healthy subjects and established monotherapy patients, not a seizure-frequency epilepsy efficacy RCT for valproate.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3130256/"},{"label":"Ben-Menachem2020 candidate","pmid":"32350749","proposed_action":"Do not add to pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links.","rationale":"This is a phase II pharmacokinetic drug-drug interaction study of cannabidiol with stiripentol or valproate in epilepsy patients, not a valproate placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32350749/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; published=Apr 13, 2026; title=DEPAKOTE ER (DIVALPROEX SODIUM) TABLET, EXTENDED RELEASE [ABBVIE INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=0dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac; effective_time=20260331; title=DEPAKOTE ER / DIVALPROEX SODIUM; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not allowed for black-box-warning verification.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%220dc024ce-efc8-4690-7cb5-639c728fccac%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Valproate Information page; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed/PMC RCT reports; ClinicalTrials.gov","reason":"Replace non-allowed or insufficient source names with trusted-source domains used in this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/valproate-information","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8559420/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI Bookshelf/StatPearls mechanism review","reason":"FDA/accessdata and NCBI sources support the mechanism wording while avoiding DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/021168s044lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559112/"]}],"summary":"Valproic acid/divalproex/sodium valproate should remain a consolidated active-moiety row. The three existing PubMed RCT links are appropriate, McGuire1988 and the cannabidiol interaction trial should not be added, and the RR50 value of 19 percentage points is verified. Required updates are source-policy cleanup for the boxed-warning/evidence fields, correction of vomiting from 23% to 27% in the adverse-event list, and minor alias/trade-name additions for FDA-listed Depakote CP/Sprinkle Capsules."}
